    "title": {
      "en": "Meadow or Tree Pipit?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Habitat and call first. Meadow Pipits live on open ground and call a thin 'tsip-tsip'. Tree Pipits live around trees and call a buzzing 'teez'. Up close, a Tree Pipit has a heavier bill, a buffy breast with bold streaks on the flank and a short, curved hind claw."
    }
  },
